      ":question/problem": "The data $C$ is given by\n$4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10$,\nand the data set $D$ is given by\n$1, 3, 4, 4, 5, 5, 6$.\nWhich of the following statements correctly compares the means of data set $C$ and data set $D$?\n\n1. The mean of the data set $C$ is less than the mean of the data set $D$.\n2. The mean of each data set is $4$.\n3. The mean of each data set is $7$.\n4. The mean of the data set $C$ is greater than the mean of the data set $D$."
