      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-288220",
      ":question/problem": "The data $M$ is given by\n$10, 15, 15, 20$,\nand the data set $N$ is given by\n$10, 15, 15, 20, 45$.\nWhich of the following statements correctly compares the means of data set $M$ and data set $N$?\n\n1. The mean of the data set $M$ is less than the mean of the data set $N$.\n2. The mean of the data set $M$ is greater than the mean of the data set $N$.\n3. The means of the data set $M$ and data set $N$ are equal.\n4. The mean of each data set is $15$."
